  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The ancient city of Petra, carved into the sandstone cliffs of Jordan, was once a major trading centre in the Middle East. The city's strategic location allowed it to control the trade routes between Arabia and the Mediterranean. However, as the Roman Empire expanded, Petra's importance began to decline. By the 4th century AD, the city had been abandoned, its intricate facades and monuments left to the mercy of the desert winds.\n\nToday, visitors can explore the ruins of Petra on foot or by horseback, taking in the breathtaking views of the surrounding landscape. The Treasury building, with its intricately carved façade, is one of the most iconic landmarks in the city. Meanwhile, the Monastery, perched atop a rugged mountain peak, offers panoramic views of the valley below.\n\nDespite being abandoned for centuries, Petra's legacy lives on through its architecture and artistry. Archaeologists have discovered numerous inscriptions and graffiti that provide valuable insights into the daily life of the ancient inhabitants. As we walk through the city's ruins, we are reminded of the ingenuity and creativity of our ancestors.\",\n\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"According to the passage, what was Petra's main function in the Middle East?\",\n      \"options\": [\"A major trading centre\", \"A centre for ancient art\", \"A place of worship\", \"A site for archaeological excavations\"],\n      \"answer\": \"A major trading centre\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What was the main reason for Petra's decline?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The city was ravaged by wars\", \"Its strategic location became less important\", \"The climate became too harsh\", \"The Roman Empire expanded and took over\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The Roman Empire expanded and took over\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What is notable about the Treasury building?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It was built by the Romans\", \"Its façade is plain and unadorned\", \"It has intricate carvings\", \"It's no longer standing\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It has intricate carvings\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the daily life of Petra's inhabitants?\",\n      \"options\": [\"They were nomadic herders\", \"They had a sophisticated system of governance\", \"They left behind valuable inscriptions and graffiti\", \"They were all skilled artists\"],\n      \"answer\": \"They left behind valuable inscriptions and graffiti\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"The author's attitude towards Petra is best described as?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Disdainful\", \"Indifferent\", \"Respectful, highlighting its ingenuity and creativity\", \"Critical\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Respectful, highlighting its ingenuity and creativity\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
